19 Q 3437 0 3386 0 L 416 0 Q 358 0 336 19 Q 314 38 314 102 L 314 365 Q 314 410 323 445 Q 333 480 371 525 Q 410 570 486 634 L 1850 1990 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" d=\"M 2362 4806 Q 2605 4806 2797 4755 Q 2989 4704 3142 4614 Q 3296 4525 3414 4416 Q 3533 4307 3610 4186 Q 3622 4160 3625 4131 Q 3629 4102 3590 4083 L 3226 3936 Q 3194 3917 3168 3933 Q 3142 3949 3130 3974 Q 2989 4141 2813 4243 Q 2637 4346 2368 4346 Q 1907 4346 1609 4122 Q 1312 3898 1171 3510 Q 1030 3123 1030 2637 Q 1030 2534 1049 2502 Q 1069 2470 1146 2509 Q 1389 2630 1670 2732 Q 1952 2835 2330 2835 Q 2822 2835 3171 2652 Q 3520 2470 3702 2156 Q 3885 1843 3885 1446 Q 3885 998 3664 656 Q 3443 314 3068 128 Q 2694 -58 2234 -58 Q 1670 -58 1264 220 Q 858 499 640 1027 Q 422 1555 422 2304 Q 422 3085 656 3645 Q 890 4205 1325 4505 Q 1760 4806 2362 4806 L 2362 4806 z\nM 2259 2387 Q 2093 2387 1885 2345 Q 1677 2304 1491 2240 Q 1306 2176 1171 2093 Q 1094 2042 1068 1987 Q 1043 1933 1043 1818 Q 1043 1587 1116 1340 Q 1190 1094 1334 876 Q 1478 659 1702 524 Q 1926 390 2234 390 Q 2534 390 2768 524 Q 3002 659 3139 896 Q 3277 1133 3277 1421 Q 3277 1690 3155 1910 Q 3034 2131 2803 2259 Q 2573 2387 2259 2387 L 2259 2387 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(106.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(323.725488 28.421333) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(112.59375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pc7fec62301\"><rect x=\"45.676437\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Patients a day","note":null},"answer":"<p>Rooms: 10 × 9 hours × 2 an hour = <b>180</b>. Doctors: 6 × 7 hours × 3 an hour = <b>126</b>.</p> <p>Demand is 160 a day. <b>Doctors are the bottleneck</b>; rooms already have spare capacity. Four more rooms would add nothing.</p>"},{"q":"How could Westmoor raise doctor capacity without hiring doctors?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Give history-taking and measurements to <b>intake nurses</b> before the doctor comes in: if doctor time falls from 20 to 15 minutes, capacity rises to 6 × 7 × 4 = <b>168</b>, above demand.</p> <p>Cost: two nurses at about $70k = $140k a year, against $600k for rooms that wouldn't help. Rooms still fit: 168 patients need 84 room-hours, against 90 available.</p>"},{"q":"What else could help?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Video appointments for follow-ups, which need no room</li><li>Reminders to cut no-shows, so doctor time isn't wasted</li><li>Longer doctor sessions on the busiest days</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't build the rooms: doctors, not rooms, limit Westmoor to about 126 patients a day against 160 requests, and the rooms can already handle 180. Hire two intake nurses to take histories and measurements, cutting doctor time to 15 minutes and lifting capacity to about 168 a day for about $140k a year. Risk: doctors must trust the nurses' notes. Next step: trial with two doctors for a month and measure appointment length.","great":["Computes capacity for both rooms and doctors","Identifies the real constraint","Rejects a fix aimed at the wrong constraint","Finds a cheaper fix that shifts work off the bottleneck"],"id":79,"slug":"westmoor-clinic"}